{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"b888df1c-6cdf-4bf8-abf7-0b437576872b","title":"Simple harmonic motion of a mass on a spring"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b888df1c-6cdf-4bf8-abf7-0b437576872b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A mass slides without friction on a horizontal spring. Displacement x is measured from equilibrium, where the spring exerts no net force.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Mass on a spring"},{"op":"figure","id":"spring","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-3.6,3],"y":[-1.8,1.5],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"wall","from":[-3.1,-0.6],"to":[-3.1,1]},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[-3.1,0.3],[-2.8,0.3],[-2.6,0.6],[-2.3,0],[-2,0.6],[-1.7,0],[-1.4,0.6],[-1.1,0],[-0.8,0.6],[-0.5,0],[-0.2,0.6],[0.1,0.3],[0.6,0.3]]},{"kind":"polyline","id":"mass","points":[[0.6,-0.1],[1.4,-0.1],[1.4,0.7],[0.6,0.7]],"closed":true,"fill":true,"label":"m"},{"kind":"segment","from":[-3.1,-0.15],"to":[2.6,-0.15]},{"kind":"segment","id":"equilibrium","from":[0,-1.4],"to":[0,1.1],"stroke":"dashed"},{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[1,0.3]},{"kind":"text","at":[0,1.3],"text":"equilibrium","size":"small"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-0.65],"to":[1,-0.65],"label":"x"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b888df1c-6cdf-4bf8-abf7-0b437576872b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Stretching the spring produces a restoring force toward equilibrium. Hooke’s law makes acceleration proportional to displacement, but opposite in direction.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"force_marks","on":"spring","marks":[{"kind":"segment","id":"force","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[-0.9,0.3],"arrow":true,"label":"F"},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[1,-0.75],"stroke":"dashed"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"hooke","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"F=-kx"},{"op":"equation","id":"acceleration","anchor":{"el":"hooke","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"ma=-kx\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad a=-\\frac{k}{m}x"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b888df1c-6cdf-4bf8-abf7-0b437576872b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The mass oscillates between minus A and plus A. Acceleration is greatest at the endpoints and zero at equilibrium, where speed is greatest.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"limits","on":"spring","marks":[{"kind":"segment","from":[-2,-1.2],"to":[2,-1.2]},{"kind":"point","id":"left_limit","at":[-2,-1.2],"label":"−A"},{"kind":"point","id":"right_limit","at":[2,-1.2],"label":"+A"},{"kind":"point","at":[0,-1.2],"label":"0"},{"kind":"segment","from":[-2,-1],"to":[-1.3,-1],"arrow":true},{"kind":"segment","from":[2,-1],"to":[1.3,-1],"arrow":true}]}],"checkpoint":{"question":"When the mass is left of equilibrium, which way does its acceleration point?","expected_gist":"Right, toward equilibrium."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"b888df1c-6cdf-4bf8-abf7-0b437576872b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Released from rest at plus A, displacement follows a cosine. A stiffer spring oscillates faster; a heavier mass takes longer to complete each cycle.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"motion","anchor":{"el":"acceleration","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"x(t)=A\\cos(\\omega t),\\qquad \\omega=\\sqrt{\\frac{k}{m}}"},{"op":"equation","id":"period","anchor":{"el":"motion","side":"below","gap":0.1},"latex":"T=\\frac{2\\pi}{\\omega}=2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{k}}"},{"op":"figure","id":"release","on":"spring","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[2,-1.65],"text":"release: v = 0","size":"small"},{"kind":"arc","center":[0,0.3],"r":1.8,"start":25,"end":155,"arrow":true,"label":"oscillation"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
